 endoscopic surgery</article-title><source>Surg Clin North Am</source><year>2008</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>1131</fpage><lpage>1148</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18790159</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Palanivelu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajan</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rangarajan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Parthasarathi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Senthilnathan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Praveenraj</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transumbilical endoscopic appendectomy in humans: on the road to NOTES: a prospective study</article-title><source>J Laparoendosc Adv Surg Tech A</source><year>2008</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>579</fpage><lpage>582</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18721008</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Palanivelu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajan</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rangarajan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Prasad</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalyanakumari</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Parthasarathi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>NOTES: transvaginal endoscopic cholecystectomy in humans-preliminary report of a case series</article-title><source>Am J Gastroenterol</source><year>2009</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>843</fpage><lpage>847</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19277024</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><label>25</label><element-citation publication-type=